<<!DOCTYPE type=`memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki` spec=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext`>>

<<^ code=`&#x0001;` from=`?` to=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/filters`>>
<<^ code=`&#x0002;`>>

```toml meta
cacheable = true
role      = "the house's named filters: the law index, course standing, waves and the memory stage as canon functions; canon only"
tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/meme"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/filters"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/api/filters"
```

\function lares.law.pins()
[subfilter{$:/config/lares/law/pins}] :intersection[lares.law[]]
\end

\function lares.law()
[subfilter{$:/config/lares/law/pins}] =[prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/]regexp[^lar:///ha\.ka\.ba/(\w|-)+/api/]!regexp[#]sort[title]] +[unique[]] :filter[regexp[^lar:///ha\.ka\.ba/(\w|-)+/api/]!regexp[#]] :filter[get[$origin-bag]regexp[^lar:///ha\.ka\.ba/bags/(oracle|lares|lararium)$]] :filter[regexp[^lar:///\S+$]]
\end

\function lares.road(state)
[tag[stage/road]] :filter[tags[]removeprefix[road/state/]match<state>]
\end

\function lares.course.citers(pattern,t)
[all[tiddlers]prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]!match<t>search:text:literal,casesensitive<t>regexp:text<pattern>] :filter[<currentTiddler>removeprefix<t>prefix[#/]then[no]else[yes]match[yes]]
\end

\function lares.course.text-uncited(t)
[<t>escaperegexp[]addsuffix[(?:\.(?!\w|-)|#/|(?!(?:-|\.|/|#))\W|$)]] :map[lares.course.citers<currentTiddler>,<t>count[]] +[match[0]]
\end

\function lares.course.uncited(t)
[<t>backlinks[]prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]!match<t>] :filter[<currentTiddler>removeprefix<t>prefix[#/]then[no]else[yes]match[yes]] +[count[]match[0]] :filter[lares.course.text-uncited<t>]
\end

\function lares.course.standing(t)
[<t>!has[proof]then[open]] :else[<t>get[proof]trim[]is[blank]then[open]] :else[lares.course.uncited<t>then[closed ash-ready]else[closed]enlist-input[]]
\end

\function lares.course(standing)
[tag[stage/course]!regexp[#]] :filter[lares.course.standing<currentTiddler>match<standing>]
\end

\function lares.waves()
[tag[stage/wave]]
\end

\function lares.stage(name)
[prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]] :filter[<currentTiddler>removeprefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]removeprefix<name>removeprefix[/]]
\end

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The house's named filters

The house filters stand here as `\function` definitions, defined for every filter the house runs: `[lares.law[]]` (the law index: the pins first, then every canon root meme under a bag's `api/` tree, each row answered from a canon layer), `[lares.law.pins[]]` (the pins that stand as canon law), `[lares.road[state]]` (the road reader until stage road items move; a later change retires it under the canon retirement law), `[lares.course[open]]` (course items whose proof reads blank), `[lares.course[closed]]` (items carrying proof), `[lares.course[ash-ready]]` (proved items without inbound citations), `[lares.waves[]]` (wave titles) and `[lares.stage[state]]` (every title under `lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/<stage>/`, slots too; `[lares.stage[state]!regexp[#]]` keeps the root memes). Citations count only from other memory-stage titles, excluding the item and its slots; literal text matches case and a whole title, with links also checked through backlinks. `lares wiki filter '[lares.law[]]'`, the wake and the MCP seat's `law_index` all run these same functions.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/names`>>

!! Why the names carry a period

TiddlyWiki resolves a user function as a filter operator only where its name holds a period (`filters/unknown.js`); a bare `law` would read as a field name. The `lares.` stem marks the house's own set.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/canon-only`>>

!! Canon only

The daemon reads this carrier's text from the canon layers (the oracle floor and the system canon bags) and builds the functions from it; a house name that fails to parse from the carrier (dropped, renamed, in a form no reader takes) reads from the floor the code holds, name by name. The carrier carries no `$:/tags/Global`, so no stock `\import` reads a shadowable copy. A working-layer tiddler that redefines `lares.law`, `lares.law.pins`, `lares.course`, its helpers, `lares.waves` or `lares.stage`, at this title or tagged `$:/tags/Global` elsewhere, changes no answer of `lares wiki filter`, the MCP `wiki_filter`, `lares wiki render` or the record port's filter ask. A filter naming any other `lares.` operator refuses by name. A raw `\import` a hand writes into its own wikitext stands outside that guarantee.

<<~/ahu>>

